The CTS's base libraries (delibs and qphelper) on Kosmos, which builds them
as DE_OS_UNIX - the POSIX layer inside the process - less the four things
that layer does not have and will not (`design.md` section 17): signals,
so no crash handler and a thread for a timer rather than a signal; a
process started by its command line, so deProcess says it cannot; a
library opened by name, so deDynamicLibrary finds nothing (lavapipe is in
the image, handed over by the platform); and Linux's own system calls, so
the processor count is sysconf's. Each change is under __kosmos__ and
leaves every other platform as it was.

